\begin{abstract}
Deploying Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models for real-time control requires compressing their vision token sequences, yet identical pruning applied to different architectures produces wildly divergent outcomes---from unscathed performance to total collapse. We trace this divergence to the vision-language connector, the module bridging the visual encoder and language backbone.

